2
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:10.180
Facing the resurgent waves of coronavirus
infections and the emergence

3
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.890
of more infectious strains,

4
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.580
community schools and governments are
wrestling with complex and high-stakes

5
00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.010
decisions balancing the benefits of
in-person schooling,

6
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.900
risks of virus spreading, and financial
burdens of consistently implementing

7
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.050
mitigation measures such as enhanced
ventilations.

8
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:33.260
Using the pandemic of COVID-19 to set the
epidemiological context,

9
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.680
we conducted scenario analyses to examine
the relationship between

10
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:42.400
reduced infection risk and increased
energy cost incurred from improved

11
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:47.360
ventilation in 111,485 public

12
00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.410
and private schools in the U.S.

13
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:54.300
Our work evaluated the different
time-varying infection risks of different

14
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.400
levels of schools and the ventilation
rates required to keep infection

15
00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.990
risk low. The energy costs,

16
00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.130
per square meter and per capita,

17
00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.010
were estimated on the national,

18
00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.030
state, and county basis for both public
and private schools,

19
00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:13.600
offering unprecedented operation
guidelines and financial implementation

20
00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:18.650
for school operation during and beyond the
COVID-19 pandemic.

21
00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.570
For the ventilation system to be
effective,

22
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.580
it must sufficiently lower the
concentration of the airborne virus

23
00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.660
to prevent the infection from spreading.

24
00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.690
The ventilation requirement,

25
00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:34.090
therefore, changes according to the volume
of air exhaled by students,

26
00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:35.910
the number of students in attendance,

27
00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.550
the climate, and the utility costs.

28
00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:43.540
The findings will help design guidelines
to operate HVAC systems to

29
00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:48.520
accommodate infection control needs and
control energy costs to facilitate

30
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:51.340
a healthy and sustainable school
environment.

31
00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:56.020
The trade-off analysis between reduced
airborne infection risks and

32
00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.520
increased energy costs under various
scenarios and interventions provide

33
00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.710
useful information for schools to prepare
for,

34
00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.790
mitigate the consequences of,

35
00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:10.650
respond to, and recover from the pandemic
and future epidemics,

36
00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.600
and further instill the awareness of
health and sustainability in research

37
00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:16.850
and policymaking.

